issues.problem:
These sentences read as grading guidance rather than an applicant's notes. They tell the system in advance:
- how to separate existing from planned resources;
- which overclaims to avoid (retrospective versus operational, timing versus concentration, outcome promises);
- where to place content, echoing ME5's 'exclusively within the Excellence section'.
The brief therefore pre-solves the dossier's main limitations and exposes rubric checks. It also writes part of the proposal's framing instead of giving an idea and constraints.

Several salient limitations are not registered:
- deep-channel transport and vertical plume structure lie outside the validation, which is the stated rationale for the brief's transects;
- no live alerts were issued and no decision threshold was tested with an agency;
- no city drainage sensor stream was used.
F09 also overstates its source: it says the design 'excluded' rare flood extremes, whereas the source says it 'did not represent the full range' of them.
